  "description": "A reminder is a still-planned occurrence of a plan whose reminder is on, within its lead time or past its date in the plan's own calendar day, oldest first; read and unread keep the first time and refuse an occurrence with no reminder; skipping or confirming ends one; the read state survives the reminder being switched off and on.",
